  "name": "Gated Triplet Call",
  "author": "Riddim Rack",
  "description": "A held note turned into a triplet bass phrase: twelve gate slots per bar, a call of hits in the first half and a thinner answer in the second, over a clean sine sub that gates with it. Play: hold F1, G1 or A#1 for a full bar of riff at 140-150 BPM; the pattern restarts on every new note. Macros: Gap Fill fills the rests between hits, Pattern Tone opens the filter and the square edge, Answer Fade mutes and darkens the second-half answer, Smear rounds the gate edges.",
